# AI Use & Cross-Reference Checklist

## Before Asking AI

- [ ] Do I have the original SAS/code/source logic?
- [ ] Do I have the relevant project requirements?
- [ ] Have I provided enough context?
- [ ] Am I asking AI to reproduce the existing logic rather than redesign it?

## After AI Generates Code

- [ ] Did I compare variables?
- [ ] Did I compare conditions?
- [ ] Did I check exclusions?
- [ ] Did I check missing-value behavior?
- [ ] Did I check thresholds?
- [ ] Did I ask the model to explain its reasoning?

## Cross-Reference

- [ ] Did I use a different model when practical?
- [ ] Did I provide the original source and generated code?
- [ ] Did I ask for specific mismatches?
- [ ] Did I investigate disagreements instead of choosing the answer I preferred?

## Validation

- [ ] Did I run the code?
- [ ] Did I compare the output against the expected/SAS output?
- [ ] Did I test relevant edge cases?
- [ ] Has a team member reviewed important changes?

## Before Committing

- [ ] Is the code understandable?
- [ ] Are important AI-assisted decisions documented?
- [ ] Does the implementation still match the original requirements?
- [ ] Am I confident because the work was tested and reviewed, rather than simply because AI said it was correct?